//! VT-02 acceptance in ureth (validator-registry design section 11: "a ureth hook test running VR
//! bytecode"; section 12: malformed-module and reentrancy acceptance completes before the VR code
//! hash is pinned anywhere).
//!
//! `testdata/vr-hook.json` is generated by unicity-pos-contracts `test/vr/VRHookState.t.sol` and
//! `tools/vr_hook_state.py`: the real `ValidatorRegistry` core (0xff..03) and its three facets, the
//! real `PoaElection` module and composer, and the test modules, deployed at their genesis
//! addresses on chain id 1337, set up per scenario, and then driven through one block's hooks
//! exactly as ureth calls them. Here each scenario is loaded into the signed test genesis, its
//! records are imported through the real `SealRegistry`, and the block is built and replayed
//! through the real block path, whose pre-execution runs `applyRootRecords` and `elect` with VR as
//! both the records custody and the election contract. The state VR and the modules end with must
//! be the state forge computed, slot for slot.
//!
//! The assertions:
//! - containment holds at the hook: a module that reverts, runs out of gas, returns malformed or
//!   oversized data, re-enters VR or serves an invalid output never invalidates the block; VR
//!   absorbs it as a fault (`elect` outcome 3) and the cursor still advances by exactly the batch;
//! - the maximum compound paths at VR's maximum accepted caps: a full H = 32 batch (healthy and
//!   exhausted), the 16-member election with the largest legal payloads, and the 16-member
//!   pointer-switch Boundary delivered a block after its Ack;
//! - fault attribution through public transactions after the hooks: 100 early publishes, a short
//!   publish, and a short then funded publish in one transaction leave VR Healthy;
//! - gas: every scenario runs within the provisional profile pins (`ElectGas`, `HookRecordGas`)
//!   with the system budget at exactly the hook envelope, and the measured costs and thresholds are
//!   reported against them (`cargo test --test vr_hook -- --nocapture`);
//! - record kinds 6 to 8 apply through the hook: a batch of Ack, Boundary, two `HolderRetirement`s
//!   and a foreign Closure, and a batch of `OutputRejected` and `SessionClosed` with the real
//!   `PoA`;
//! - the module pointer switches through the hook (`PoaElection` to a fresh instance, and to a
//!   module whose attach fails).

